sn22.96:2.1 | S: Then the Buddha, picking up a lump of cow dung, said to the mendicant: | T: Then the Blessed One took up a little lump of cowdung in his hand and said to that bhikkhu:
sn22.96:2.2 | S: “There’s not even this much of any incarnation that’s permanent, everlasting, eternal, imperishable, and will last forever and ever. | T: “Bhikkhu, there is not even this much individual existence that is permanent, stable, eternal, not subject to change, and that will remain the same just like eternity itself.
