sn22.96:3.1 | S: Once upon a time I was an anointed aristocratic king. | T: “In the past, bhikkhu, I was a head-anointed khattiya king.
sn22.96:3.2 | S: I had 84,000 cities, with the capital Kusāvatī the foremost. | T: I had 84,000 cities, the chief of which was the capital Kusavati.
sn22.96:3.3 | S: I had 84,000 palaces, with the Palace of Principle the foremost. | T: I had 84,000 palaces, the chief of which was the palace named Dhamma.
sn22.96:3.4 | S: I had 84,000 chambers, with the Chamber of the Grand Tower the foremost. | T: I had 84,000 halls with peaked roofs, the chief of which was the hall named the Great Array.
sn22.96:3.5 | S: I had 84,000 couches made of ivory or heartwood or gold or silver, spread with woolen covers—shag-piled or embroidered with flowers—and spread with a fine deer hide, with a canopy above and red pillows at both ends. | T: I had 84,000 couches made of ivory, of heartwood, of gold and silver, decked with long-haired coverlets, embroidered with flowers, with choice spreads made of antelope hides, with red awnings overhead and red cushions at both ends.
sn22.96:3.6 | S: I had 84,000 bull elephants with gold adornments and banners, covered with snow gold netting, with the royal bull elephant named Sabbath the foremost. | T: “I had 84,000 bull elephants with golden ornaments and golden banners, covered with nets of golden thread, the chief of which was the royal bull elephant named Uposatha.
sn22.96:3.7 | S: I had 84,000 horses with gold adornments and banners, covered with snow gold netting, with the royal steed named Thundercloud the foremost. | T: I had 84,000 steeds with golden ornaments and golden banners, covered with nets of golden thread, the chief of which was the royal steed named Valahaka.
sn22.96:3.8 | S: I had 84,000 chariots with gold adornments and banners, covered with snow gold netting, with the chariot named Triumph the foremost. | T: I had 84,000 chariots with golden ornaments and golden banners, covered with nets of golden thread, the chief of which was the chariot named Vejayanta.
sn22.96:3.9 | S: I had 84,000 jewels, with the jewel-treasure the foremost. | T: “I had 84,000 jewels, the chief of which was the jewel-gem.
sn22.96:3.10 | S: I had 84,000 women, with Queen Subhaddā the foremost. | T: I had 84,000 women, the chief of whom was Queen Subhadda.
sn22.96:3.11 | S: I had 84,000 aristocrat vassals, with the commander-treasure the foremost. | T: I had 84,000 vassals of the khattiya caste, the chief of whom was the commander-gem.
sn22.96:3.12 | S: I had 84,000 milk cows with muslin halter and bronze pails. | T: I had 84,000 cows with tethers of fine jute and milk pails of bronze.
sn22.96:3.13 | S: I had 8,400,000,000 cloths of delicate linen, cotton, silk, and wool. | T: I had 84,000 koṭis of garments made of fine linen, of fine silk, of fine wool, of fine cotton.
sn22.96:3.14 | S: I had 84,000 servings of food, which were presented to me as offerings at daybreak and dusk. | T: I had 84,000 plates on which my meals were served both in the morning and in the evening.
sn22.96:4.1 | S: Of those 84,000 cities, I only stayed in one, the capital Kusāvatī. | T: “Of those 84,000 cities, bhikkhu, there was only one city in which I resided at that time: the capital Kusavati.
sn22.96:4.2 | S: Of those 84,000 palaces, I only dwelt in one, the Palace of Principle. | T: Of those 84,000 palaces, there was only one palace in which I resided at that time: the palace named Dhamma.
sn22.96:4.3 | S: Of those 84,000 chambers, I only dwelt in one, the  Chamber of the Grand Tower. | T: Of those 84,000 halls with peaked roof, there was only one hall with peaked roof in which I resided at that time: the hall named the Great Array.
sn22.96:4.4 | S: Of those 84,000 couches, I only used one, made of ivory or heartwood or gold or silver. | T: Of those 84,000 couches, there was only one couch that I used at that time, one made either of ivory or of heartwood or of gold or of silver.
sn22.96:4.5 | S: Of those 84,000 bull elephants, I only rode one, the royal bull elephant named Sabbath. | T: “Of those 84,000 elephants, there was only one elephant that I rode at that time, the royal bull elephant named Uposatha.
sn22.96:4.6 | S: Of those 84,000 horses, I only rode one, the royal horse named Thundercloud. | T: Of those 84,000 steeds, there was only one steed that I rode at that time, the royal steed named Valahaka.
sn22.96:4.7 | S: Of those 84,000 chariots, I only rode one, the chariot named Triumph. | T: Of those 84,000 chariots, there was only one chariot that I rode in at that time, the chariot named Vejayanta.
sn22.96:4.8 | S: Of those 84,000 women, I was only served by one, an aristocrat maiden or a coquette. | T: “Of those 84,000 women, there was only one woman who waited on me at that time, either a khattiya maiden or a velamika maiden.
sn22.96:4.9 | S: Of those 8,400,000,000 cloths, I only wore one pair, made of delicate linen, cotton, silk, and wool. | T: Of those 84,000 koṭis of garments, there was only one pair of garments that I wore at that time, one made either of fine linen or of fine silk or of fine wool or of fine cotton.
sn22.96:4.10 | S: Of those 84,000 servings of food, I only had one, eating at most a cup of rice with suitable sauce. | T: Of those 84,000 plates, there was only one plate from which I ate at most a measure of rice with a suitable curry.
sn22.96:4.11 | S: And so all those conditioned phenomena have passed, ceased, and perished. | T: “Thus, bhikkhu, all those formations have passed, ceased, changed.
sn22.96:4.12 | S: So impermanent are conditions, | T: So impermanent are formations, bhikkhu,
sn22.96:4.13 | S: so unstable are conditions, | T: so unstable,
sn22.96:4.14 | S: so unreliable are conditions. | T: so unreliable.
sn22.96:4.15 | S: This is quite enough for you to become disillusioned, dispassionate, and freed regarding all conditions.” | T: It is enough, bhikkhu, to feel revulsion towards all formations, enough to become dispassionate towards them, enough to be liberated from them.”
sn22.96:4.16 | P: Catutthaṁ. | T: (none)

